==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|neep}}, from {{inh|en|ang|nǣp|t=turnip, rape}}, borrowed from {{der|en|la|nāpus}}. Compare {{noncog|is|næpa|t=turnip}}.

Cognate with {{cog|en|turnip}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|Scotland}} The [[swede]] ([[rutabaga]]); [[turnip]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1934|author=w:Lewis Grassic Gibbon|title=Grey Granite|publisher=Polygon|year_published=2006|series=A Scots Quair|page=494
|passage=Poor Mr Piddle with his long think neck and his long thin head, as bald as a '''neep''' and something the shape {{...}}}}

